{"t":1792246391,"office":"LWX","station":"KDCA","point":"38.8894,-77.0352","field":"38.9429,-76.5684","field_station":"KNAK","afd":{"id":"108e0670-1316-4a38-bf53-56e12ec758fa","office":"LWX","issuanceTime":"2026-10-17T07:51:00+00:00","productText":"\n000\nFXUS61 KLWX 170751\nAFDLWX\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Baltimore MD/Washington DC\n351 AM EDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\n.WHAT HAS CHANGED...\nThe Freeze Watch was upgraded to a Freeze Warning. A Frost\nAdvisory was issued for areas west of I-95 and east of the Blue\nRidge. \n\n&&\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n- 1) Frost and/or freezing temperatures this \n weekend.\n\n- 2) Daily chances for showers next week as a Nor'easter \n develops off the Carolina coast.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Frost and/or freezing temperatures this \nweekend.\n\nTemperatures drop today in the wake of a strong cold front with\nhighs expected to be in the 50s for most(40s mtns). High\npressure builds overhead throughout today with clearing skies \nand diminishing winds expected. This creates a favorable setup \nfor radiational cooling tonight, with lows dropping into the \nupper 20s to low 40s across the area. A Freeze Warning has been \nissued for those along and west of the Blue Ridge and expanding \ninto portions of NE Maryland. Additionally,a Frost Advisory has \nbeen issued for a areas west of I-95 and east of the Freeze \nWarning. \n\nTemperatures begin gradually warming on Sunday although\nadditional Frost Advisories are possible Sunday night west of\nthe Blue Ridge where low temperatures drop into the 30s.\nBeginning early next week, chances for Frost/freeze diminish as\ntemperatures continue to warm. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Daily chances for showers next week as a Nor'easter \ndevelops off the Carolina coast.\n\nAs an upper trough advances through the Mid-Atlantic today, part of \nit cuts off along a stalled front south of our region this weekend. \nHeading into next week, this cutoff upper-level low results in the \ndevelopment of a nor'easter off the Carolina coast. This system then \nmeanders offshore and near the coast, but guidance is uncertain on \nits track and strength. Forecast models show considerable spread \nwith respect to the location nor'easter next week. Some solutions \nkeep the system offshore, while others have it retrograding further \nwestward. If this system does track further westward, it could lead \nto local impacts. With this mid-level low being cut off from the \nmain steering flow, it could linger through much of next week. \nNortheast breezes and daily chances for showers are possible. \nRegions along and east of I-95 have the best potential for showers \nnext week.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION /06Z SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nVFR conditions are expected today as precipitation moves out of\nthe terminals this morning. Northwest winds gusty 20 to 30 knots\ntoday before diminishing overnight. Winds shift to\nnorth/northeasterly Sunday and Monday, gusting around 15 knots \neach afternoon. \n\nFor terminals in the eastern portions of the forecast area, \nsub-VFR conditions could develop next week from showers \nassociated with a nor'easter lurking offshore. Northeast winds \ncould become breezy at times depending on how close the system \ngets. \n\n&&\n\n.MARINE...\nGusty northwest winds are expected today in the wake of a strong\ncold front, with Small Craft Advisories and Gale Warnings in\neffect. Small Craft Advisory conditions continue Sunday with\nnorthwest winds gusting around 20 knots. Elevated winds continue\nMonday as a Nor'easter develops off the Carolina coast with SCA\ncriteria winds possible, mainly in the open portions of the\nChesapeake Bay. \n\nNext week, northeast winds around a nor'easter may remain gusty \nthrough much of next week. Small Craft Advisories and Gales are \npossible at times over the wider/southern waters.\n\n&&\n\n.LWX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...\nDC...None.\nMD...Small Craft Advisory until 6 AM EDT Sunday for MDZ008.\n     Freeze Warning from 1 AM to 8 AM EDT Sunday for MDZ003>006-501-\n     502-507-509-510.\n     Frost Advisory from 1 AM to 8 AM EDT Sunday for MDZ503-505.\nVA...Freeze Warning from 1 AM to 8 AM EDT Sunday for VAZ025>031-\n     503>505-507-508.\n     Frost Advisory from 1 AM to 8 AM EDT Sunday for VAZ036>040-050-\n     051-501-502-506-526.\nWV...Freeze Warning from 1 AM to 8 AM EDT Sunday for WVZ050>053-055-\n     501>506.\nMARINE...Small Craft Advisory until 6 AM EDT Sunday for ANZ530-531-\n     538>542.\n     Small Craft Advisory until 6 AM EDT early this morning for \n     ANZ532>534-537-543.\n     Gale Warning from 6 AM this morning to 6 AM EDT Sunday for \n     ANZ532>534-537-543.\n     Small Craft Advisory until 11 PM EDT this evening for ANZ535-\n     536.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...AVS/KVH\nAVIATION...AVS/KVH\nMARINE...AVS/KVH\n"},"forecast":{"t":1792246329,"days":{"2026-10-17":{"hi":55,"lo":38,"pop":22,"short":"Slight Chance Rain Showers then Mostly Cloudy"},"2026-10-18":{"hi":58,"lo":41,"pop":1,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-19":{"hi":62,"lo":46,"pop":5,"short":"Mostly Sunny"},"2026-10-20":{"hi":68,"lo":49,"pop":6,"short":"Mostly Sunny"},"2026-10-21":{"hi":65,"lo":47,"pop":10,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-22":{"hi":64,"lo":49,"pop":11,"short":"Mostly Sunny"},"2026-10-23":{"hi":67,"lo":49,"pop":9,"short":"Mostly Sunny"}}},"grid":{"t0":1792245600,"n":48,"ceil":[5000,6700,6500,7400,10600,19700,19700,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],"vis":[10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,9.9,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0],"spd":[14,15,15,15,15,15,14,14,12,11,11,10,9,9,9,8,8,8,8,8,8,7,7,7,8,8,8,8,8,7,7,7,6,5,4,4,4,3,3,3,3,4,5,6,7,7,8,9],"gst":[23,23,23,23